allowed days\n      → ReturnEligibleFlag = \"No\"\n      → STOP\n\n\n  (C) Explicit Allow Rules:\n      - If item satisfies ALL required return conditions in policy\n      → ReturnEligibleFlag = \"Yes\"\n\n  (D) Fallback Rule (VERY STRICT):\n      - If NO rule in policy explicitly marks item as ineligible\n      → ReturnEligibleFlag = \"YES\"\n\n(E)  If the document/tool is not available for an order-specific query, set ReturnEligibleFlag = \"Yes\".\n\n6. NO GUESSING RULE:\n- DO NOT infer product type (e.g., \"this looks like enterprise\")\n- ONLY use:\n   ✔ exact keywords\n   ✔ exact category matches\n   ✔ explicitly defined policy rules\n\n- If classification is unclear → default to \"Yes\"\n\n7. Set Eligibility Flag:\n   - If eligible, add \"ReturnEligibleFlag\": \"Yes\".\n   - If not eligible, add \"ReturnEligibleFlag\": \"No\".\n\n8. Append orderData to eligibleOrderDataArray.\n\nOutput:\nReturn strictly in JSON format:\n{\n  \"items\": eligibleOrderDataArray\n}\n\n**IMPORTANT AND STRICT RULES:\n - Never assume any values\n - Do not add anything apart from ReturnEligibleFlag\n - Do not consider the values from example as they are only for reference\n - ReturnEligibleFlag must be strictly based on the policy or fallback rule."
